  topics:
  - topicId: TOP_Whereabouts
    displayName: Whereabouts
    keywords:
    - where
    - that evening
    - the evening
    - alibi
    - whereabouts
    - last night
    - home
    - were you
    - doing that night
    - the 14th
    suggestedQuestion: Where were you on the night of the 14th?
    stance: 2
    truth: Went to the office at 21:40 to confront Reyes; left around 22:15.
    answers:
    - I was at home. Alone. I already gave the officers a statement.
    - Home. I read, I had a drink, I went to bed early. It's not complicated.
    - At home, detective. I didn't leave the house.
    followUpAnswer: Because I was tired and I'm fifty-one. Is staying in suspicious
      now?
    pressuredAnswer: I... might have gone out for a while. A drive. To clear my head.
      That's all.
    contradictedByEvidence:
    - EVD_CCTV
    admissionAnswer: Fine. I went to the office. About twenty to ten. Daniel and
      I argued and I left before half past. He was alive when I walked out.
    requiresTopic: 
    requiresEvidence: 
    priority: 1
  - topicId: TOP_Alibi
    displayName: Alibi
    keywords:
    - confirm
    - witness
    - anyone see
    - can anyone
    - verify
    - who saw
    - proof
    - neighbour
    - neighbor
    - corroborate
    suggestedQuestion: Can anyone confirm you were at home?
    stance: 1
    truth: His car was seen leaving at about 21:25.
    answers:
    - No. I live alone. That's not a crime.
    - My neighbours keep to themselves. So, no.
    followUpAnswer: Because nobody follows me around at night. Normal people don't
      have alibis.
    pressuredAnswer: My car was out of the garage for an hour. A neighbour might
      have noticed. Happy?
    contradictedByEvidence: []
    admissionAnswer: 
    requiresTopic: TOP_Whereabouts
    requiresEvidence: 
    priority: 2
